  "notes": "Warren J. Smith, Modern Lens Design, 2nd ed., Figure 20.6 (zoom), p. 390. Multi-configuration model: configuration 1 = short, 2 = mid, 3 = long. Book values by configuration: [short] Figure 20.6 short, p. 390. Book: EFL 70.58, BFL 102, NA -0.0075 (F/66.8), GIH 17.17 (HFOV=13.67), PTZ/F 3.94, VL 38.76, infinite conjugate. [mid] Figure 20.6 mid, p. 391. Book: EFL 100, BFL 98.95, NA -0.0053 (F/94.6), GIH 24.33 (HFOV=13.67), PTZ/F 2.779, VL 38.76, infinite conjugate. [long] Figure 20.6 long, p. 392. Book: EFL 141.6, BFL 101.9, NA -0.0037 (F/133.9), GIH 34.44 (HFOV=13.67), PTZ/F 1.963, VL 38.76, infinite conjugate. [end] Wavelengths 0.6328 um as in the book (primary first). Stop at surface 1 (the book's plane air surface). Zoom lens: the configurations are the zoom positions the book lists (short, mid, long); the per-position files Figure 20.6 short/mid/long.lens.json hold the same data one position per file. The multi-configuration table sets THIC 3, THIC 7, THIC 9, THIC 11. The book lists two dummy plane air surfaces after surface 9, with thicknesses equal to the air spaces after surfaces 3 and 7 (3.058 and 13.049) and sa 0.0, printed without a sign. Only negative values reproduce the book's VL 38.76 and its drawing, so they are folded into the air space after surface 9: 17.973 - 3.058 - 13.049 = 1.866. (These are the numbers of the short position; the mid and long positions are folded the same way.) The stop is the front plane surface (book sa 0.0); its 1.057 diameter follows from the book's EFL and F-number, the same in every position. Book lists sa 0.0 on some surfaces; left as automatic semi-diameter.",
